WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.440
very specific outcome that is looking increasingly

00:03.440 --> 00:05.280
unrealistic.

00:05.280 --> 00:06.760
This is what I think is really annoying.

00:06.760 --> 00:08.120
This blew my mind.

00:08.120 --> 00:09.960
This is from Morningstar.

00:09.960 --> 00:13.560
The S&P global ratings assigned these bonds.

00:13.560 --> 00:16.080
So the loans that these private equity companies

00:16.080 --> 00:19.240
are taking out to fund these data centers,

00:19.240 --> 00:24.400
they assigned the bonds of investment grade rating of A+.

00:24.400 --> 00:29.440
However, the debt yield is 6.58%.

00:29.440 --> 00:31.360
OK.

00:31.360 --> 00:35.880
That rate is typically associated with junk bonds.

00:35.880 --> 00:38.480
So they're saying it's A+.

00:38.480 --> 00:40.480
But what are their actions showing?

00:40.480 --> 00:42.400
What does this remind you of?

00:42.400 --> 00:45.440
Like this is the plot of a movie and a book

00:45.440 --> 00:47.680
and something that actually happened.

00:47.680 --> 00:48.400
I wrote.

00:48.400 --> 00:50.120
It's giving subprime mortgages.

00:50.120 --> 00:50.600
Yeah.

00:50.600 --> 00:53.080
I know when I was reading this, I was like, God, this is,

00:53.080 --> 00:56.080
I feel like I'm reading about the subprime mortgage crisis

00:56.080 --> 00:59.160
in a book about the subprime mortgage crisis.

00:59.160 --> 01:01.560
But it's happening right in front of me.

